.Dd May 5, 2025
.Dt HWC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hwc
.Nd Instrumentation tool for hardware counters.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Op Fl cfh
.Op Fl c Ar backend name
.Op Fl f Ar config
.Op Fl h
.Op Ar path to executable
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
uses kernel facilities provided by the
.Xr hwc 4
framework to launch and count events occuired during runtime of an executable
specified by
.Pa path
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "event_payload"
.It Fl c Ar name
Optional. Name of the tracing backend to be used.
Currently supported tracing backends are:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
pmu (riscv)
.El
.Pp
.Nm
will select the first available backend if the flag is not present.
.It Fl f Ar config
Configuration file.
.It Fl h
Usage information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Count events occured during execution of a program:
.Pp
.Dl "hwc -f hwc-x730 /usr/bin/uname"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hwc 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
